# Facets

## Facet Wrap

### Basic Histogram using `Weight`

```{r hist-1}
# Basic histogram
ggplot(NFL, aes(x = Weight)) +
  geom_histogram()
```

### Histogram with Fill using `PositionGrp` OR `Side`

Choose ONE: `fill = PositionGrp` or `fill = Side`

I chose `Side`.

```{r hist-2}
# Add fill
ggplot(NFL, aes(x = Weight, fill = Side)) +
  geom_histogram()
```

### Histogram using `facet_wrap()` with `PositionGrp`

```{r hist-3}
# facet_wrap by PositionGrp
ggplot(NFL, aes(x = Weight)) +
  geom_histogram() +
  facet_wrap(~ PositionGrp)
```

### Histogram using `facet_grid()` with `Side`

```{r hist-4}
# facet_grid by Side
ggplot(NFL, aes(x = Weight)) +
  geom_histogram() +
  facet_grid(Side ~ .)
```

### Quick interpretation (2–3 sentences)

Pick one faceted plot and write what pattern you notice.

**Answer:** In the faceted PositionGrp plot, player weights look different depending on their position group. Some groups tend to have heavier players while others have more players at lower weights. Separating the groups into their own plots makes these differences much easier to notice.

